---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="About Us | ChemistryDesk Laboratory Suite" 
  description="About ChemistryDesk: Our mission to provide open-access, zero-lag computational chemistry tools for researchers and students."
>
  <main style="max-width: 800px; margin: 3rem auto; padding: 0 1.5rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #334155; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;">
    <h1 style="color: #0f172a; font-size: 2.25rem; font-weight: 800; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">About ChemistryDesk</h1>
    <p style="color: #64748b; font-size: 0.875rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">Dedicated to Accessible Benchtop Computational Chemistry</p>

    <section style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <h2 style="color: #0f172a; font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700;">Our Mission</h2>
      <p>ChemistryDesk was founded to address a persistent gap in standard laboratory workflows: everyday computational tasks—such as crystal hydration mass compensation, serial dilution ladders, and powder XRD line broadening calculations—are often trapped behind paid software licenses, slow mobile apps, or cluttered, ad-heavy portals.</p>
      <p>Our platform delivers clean, instantaneous, client-side scientific calculators paired directly with rigorous theoretical background, mathematical derivations, and practical benchtop Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs).</p>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <h2 style="color: #0f172a; font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700;">Editorial Standards & Accuracy</h2>
      <p>Every computational engine deployed on ChemistryDesk is engineered using standard analytical principles:</p>
      <ul style="margin-left: 1.5rem; margin-top: 0.5rem;">
        <li>Standard atomic weights adhere to current IUPAC periodic table standards.</li>
        <li>Physical crystallographic equations (such as the Scherrer formula) account for instrument broadening and exact radiation source wavelengths.</li>
        <li>Solution preparation formulas explicitly calculate hydration state additions ($MW_{\text{eff}} = MW_{\text{base}} + n \cdot 18.015\text{ g/mol}$) to eliminate negative concentration errors on the benchtop.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <h2 style="color: #0f172a; font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700;">Platform Architecture</h2>
      <p>ChemistryDesk is built using modern static web architectures (Astro) deployed to global edge networks. This ensures that calculations load in milliseconds, consume minimal device memory, and function securely without tracking proprietary laboratory data.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>